   'time',
   'McCartney honors Deputy Daniel McCartney, 34, of Pierce County, Washington, a decorated U.S. Navy veteran from Loyalton, California. He died in the line of duty on Jan. 8, 2018, from gunshot wounds received during a foot pursuit after responding to an armed burglary.

You do this one as a team of three. The team rows 2,000 m, then works through 14 dumbbell thrusters (50 lb / 35 lb), 34 kettlebell swings (70 lb / 53 lb), 484 double-unders and 108 burpees, rows another 2,000 m and finishes with 18 deadlifts (225 lb / 155 lb). The 484 double-unders are the big block, so a team with steady jump ropes moves fastest. CrossFit does not say how to split the work, so agree on a plan before you start.',
   '[{"name": "Row", "reps": "2,000 m", "tip": "Share the distance in short turns so the rower never sits empty."}, {"name": "Dumbbell Thrusters", "reps": "14", "tip": "Hold a dumbbell on each shoulder, squat below parallel and drive straight up to lockout overhead.", "rx_men": "50 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}, {"name": "Kettlebell Swings", "reps": "34", "tip": "Snap your hips and let the bell float up. CrossFit''s standard swing finishes overhead.", "rx_men": "70 lb", "rx_women": "53 lb"}, {"name": "Double-Unders", "reps": "484", "tip": "Small, quick jumps and fast wrists. Swap jumpers before anyone starts tripping."}, {"name": "Burpees", "reps": "108", "tip": "Chest to the floor, then a small jump at the top. Keep each turn short."}, {"name": "Row", "reps": "2,000 m", "tip": "Tired arms now. Drive with the legs and keep the turns short."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "18", "tip": "Flat back, bar close to your shins, stand all the way up.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your team''s finish time.',
   '["Agree on how you will split the work before you start", "Swap often on the double-unders", "Save something for the second 2,000 m row"]'::jsonb,
   '["Decide whether one or more partners can work at once, because CrossFit does not say.", "Set a rep count for each turn, such as 50 double-unders or 10 burpees, and swap without talking it over.", "Keep turns on the rower to about 250 m so the stroke stays strong.", "On the kettlebell swings, keep your arms loose and let your hips do the lifting.", "Brace hard before each deadlift and set the bar down under control."]'::jsonb,
   'Use lighter weights, such as 35 lb / 20 lb dumbbells, a 53 lb / 35 lb kettlebell and 155 lb / 105 lb deadlifts. Replace double-unders with single-unders at twice the count, or cut them to 242. Shorten each row to 1,000 m if time is a concern.',
   '[{"question": "What is the McCartney workout?", "answer": "For time in teams of 3: 2,000 m row, 14 dumbbell thrusters, 34 kettlebell swings, 484 double-unders, 108 burpees, 2,000 m row and 18 deadlifts. Loads are 50 lb / 35 lb dumbbells, a 70 lb / 53 lb kettlebell and 225 lb / 155 lb deadlifts."}, {"question": "How should a team split McCartney?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Agree on a plan before you start, such as one person working at a time with short turns, and note it with your time."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in McCartney?", "answer": "658 reps (14 thrusters, 34 swings, 484 double-unders, 108 burpees and 18 deadlifts) plus 4,000 m of rowing."}, {"question": "Who was McCartney?", "answer": "Deputy Daniel McCartney, 34, of Pierce County, Washington, a decorated U.S. Navy veteran. He died in the line of duty on Jan. 8, 2018, after responding to an armed burglary."}]'::jsonb,
