   'time',
   'Meadows honors U.S. Marine Corps Capt. Joshua S. Meadows, 30, of Bastrop, Texas, of the 1st Marine Special Operations Battalion, Marine Corps Forces Special Operations Command. He was killed by enemy fire on Sept. 5, 2009, in Farah Province, Afghanistan.

Everything happens on a set of rings. You do 20 muscle-ups, 25 slow lowers from an inverted hang with a straight body and straight arms, 30 ring handstand push-ups, 35 ring rows and 40 ring push-ups. That is 150 reps, and the first three movements are among the hardest skills in gymnastics. The order is cruel: by the time you reach the ring rows and push-ups, your arms and shoulders are already spent.',
   '[{"name": "Muscle-Ups", "reps": "20", "tip": "Keep the rings close, pull to your chest and turn over quickly into the dip."}, {"name": "Inverted Hang Lowers", "reps": "25", "tip": "Start upside down on the rings, then lower slowly with a straight body and straight arms. CrossFit does not say where each lower ends."}, {"name": "Ring Handstand Push-Ups", "reps": "30", "tip": "Turn the rings out a little at the top and lower under control. Keep your body tight."}, {"name": "Inverted Rows", "reps": "35", "tip": "Ring rows: walk your feet forward, keep your body straight and pull your chest to the rings."}, {"name": "Ring Push-Ups", "reps": "40", "tip": "Hold the rings steady, chest to ring height, and lock your arms out at the top."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Break the muscle-ups into small sets from the start", "Go slow on the lowers, that is the point", "Set the rings low for the rows and push-ups"]'::jsonb,
   '["Plan the 20 muscle-ups as sets of 2 to 4 so you do not fail early.", "On the lowers, squeeze your glutes and keep your arms locked the whole way down.", "CrossFit does not say where each lower should end, so pick a finish point, such as a hang or the floor, and keep it the same.", "Ring handstand push-ups need a strap or a very steady setup; practice them on another day before you try this one.", "Set up a second pair of rings at low height if you can, so you do not have to change them before the rows."]'::jsonb,
   'Replace muscle-ups with pull-ups and ring dips, or jumping muscle-ups. For the lowers, do slow skin-the-cats or tuck lowers with bent knees. Replace ring handstand push-ups with handstand push-ups against a wall or pike push-ups. Raise your feet less on the ring rows, and do ring push-ups on your knees or push-ups on the floor. Cut every set in half for a shorter workout.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Meadows workout?", "answer": "For time: 20 muscle-ups, 25 slow lowers from an inverted hang on the rings with a straight body and arms, 30 ring handstand push-ups, 35 ring rows and 40 ring push-ups."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Meadows?", "answer": "150 reps, all on the rings."}, {"question": "What counts as a lower from an inverted hang?", "answer": "Start upside down on the rings and lower slowly with your body straight and your arms straight. CrossFit does not say where the lower ends, so keep your finish point the same on every rep."}, {"question": "Who was Meadows?", "answer": "U.S. Marine Corps Capt. Joshua S. Meadows, 30, of Bastrop, Texas, of the 1st Marine Special Operations Battalion. He was killed by enemy fire on Sept. 5, 2009, in Farah Province, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
