   'full-body',
   array['running','barbell']::text[],
   'time',
   'Miron honors Mirosław "Miron" Łucki, 38, of the Polish Army, who died on Aug. 23, 2013, in Ghazni Province, Afghanistan, from wounds caused by an improvised explosive device. He was a Warrant Officer and was posthumously promoted to Sergeant Major of the Army. He loved cross-country running and the intensity of CrossFit workouts.

You do 5 rounds of an 800 m run, 23 back squats at three-quarters of your body weight and 13 deadlifts at one and a half times your body weight. That is 4,000 m of running, 115 back squats and 65 deadlifts. Because the loads are set by body weight, the workout scales to everyone, but it never gets light. The runs give you little rest before the next heavy set.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Hold a steady pace. Your legs need to be ready for the squats when you get back."}, {"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "23", "tip": "Bar on your upper back, squat below parallel and stand tall. Break the set before your form slips.", "rx_men": "¾ body weight", "rx_women": "¾ body weight"}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "13", "tip": "Flat back, bar close to your legs. Short sets or quick singles work at this weight.", "rx_men": "1½ body weight", "rx_women": "1½ body weight"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Load the bars before you start", "Break the 23 squats early, such as 8, 8 and 7", "Run at a pace you can hold for all 5 rounds"]'::jsonb,
   '["Use two barbells if you can, because the deadlift is twice the squat weight.", "Rack the squat bar at shoulder height so you can step under it without wasting energy.", "Brace before every deadlift rep and reset your back if it starts to round.", "Use the first minute of each run to bring your breathing back down.", "Keep the same set plan every round so you can tell when you are slowing down."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the squat to half your body weight and the deadlift to your body weight, or less. Cut each round to 15 back squats and 9 deadlifts, shorten the runs to 400 m, or do 3 rounds instead of 5.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Miron workout?", "answer": "5 rounds for time of an 800 m run, 23 back squats at ¾ body weight and 13 deadlifts at 1½ body weight."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Miron?", "answer": "180 reps: 115 back squats and 65 deadlifts, plus 4,000 m of running."}, {"question": "How do I work out the loads?", "answer": "Multiply your body weight by 0.75 for the back squat and by 1.5 for the deadlift. A 180 lb athlete uses 135 lb and 270 lb."}, {"question": "Who was Miron?", "answer": "Mirosław \"Miron\" Łucki, 38, of the Polish Army. He died on Aug. 23, 2013, in Ghazni Province, Afghanistan, from wounds caused by an improvised explosive device, and was posthumously promoted to Sergeant Major of the Army."}]'::jsonb,
