   'time',
   'Monti honors U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Jared C. Monti, 30, of Raynham, Massachusetts, of the 3rd Squadron, 71st Cavalry, 10th Mountain Division. He was killed on June 21, 2006, during combat operations in Gowardesh, Afghanistan, and was awarded the Medal of Honor on Sept. 17, 2009.

Each of the 5 rounds is 50 barbell step-ups (45 lb / 35 lb to a 20 in box), 15 cleans (135 lb / 95 lb), another 50 step-ups and 10 snatches at the same weight. That is 500 step-ups, 75 cleans and 50 snatches. The step-ups grind your legs down slowly, so the cleans and snatches get harder every round. This is a long, steady workout, not a sprint.',
   '[{"name": "Barbell Step-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Bar on your back, whole foot on the box and stand all the way up. Switch legs as you go.", "rx_men": "45 lb, 20 in", "rx_women": "35 lb, 20 in"}, {"name": "Cleans", "reps": "15", "tip": "Pull from the floor and catch the bar on your shoulders. CrossFit does not say power or squat clean.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}, {"name": "Barbell Step-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Same rhythm as the first set. Count in tens to stay on track.", "rx_men": "45 lb, 20 in", "rx_women": "35 lb, 20 in"}, {"name": "Snatches", "reps": "10", "tip": "Bar from the floor to overhead in one motion. CrossFit does not say power or squat snatch.", "rx_men": "135 lb", "rx_women": "95 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Find a step-up rhythm you can keep for 500 reps", "Do the cleans and snatches as quick singles", "Use two barbells to save time"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set up the light step-up bar and the heavy bar side by side, so moving between them is quick.", "Drive through the heel of the foot on the box, and do not push off the floor with the back leg.", "CrossFit does not say whether the step-ups count per leg; count each time you stand on the box as one rep.", "Treat each snatch as a single and reset your feet and back before every pull.", "Wrap the bar pad or use a towel if the step-up bar bothers your neck over 500 reps."]'::jsonb,
   'Use an empty training bar or no bar for the step-ups, or a lower box. Lower the cleans and snatches to 95 lb / 65 lb or less, and use power snatches or dumbbell snatches if the barbell snatch is new to you. Cut each set of step-ups to 25, or do 3 rounds instead of 5.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Monti workout?", "answer": "5 rounds for time of 50 barbell step-ups, 15 cleans, 50 barbell step-ups and 10 snatches. The step-up bar is 45 lb / 35 lb to a 20 in box; the cleans and snatches are 135 lb / 95 lb."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Monti?", "answer": "625 reps: 500 barbell step-ups, 75 cleans and 50 snatches."}, {"question": "Do the cleans and snatches have to be squat or power?", "answer": "CrossFit just says cleans and snatches. Pick the style you can do safely and keep it the same every round."}, {"question": "Who was Monti?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Jared C. Monti, 30, of Raynham, Massachusetts, of the 10th Mountain Division. He was killed on June 21, 2006, in Gowardesh, Afghanistan, and was awarded the Medal of Honor in 2009."}]'::jsonb,
