   'time',
   'Morrison honors U.S. Army Spc. Scott Morrison, 23, of Blue Ash, Ohio, of the 584th Mobility Augmentation Company, 20th Engineer Battalion. He died on Sept. 26, 2010, from injuries suffered the day before when insurgents attacked his vehicle with an improvised explosive device in Kandahar, Afghanistan.

You do 50, 40, 30, 20 and 10 reps of wall balls (20 lb / 14 lb ball to a 10 ft / 9 ft target), box jumps (24 in / 20 in) and kettlebell swings (53 lb / 35 lb). That is 150 reps of each movement, 450 in all. None of the weights are heavy, but the big early sets burn your legs and lungs. Once you reach the set of 30, the end comes quickly.',
   '[{"name": "Wall Balls", "reps": "50-40-30-20-10", "tip": "Squat below parallel and drive the ball to the target. Catch it high and go straight into the next rep.", "rx_men": "20 lb, 10 ft", "rx_women": "14 lb, 9 ft"}, {"name": "Box Jumps", "reps": "50-40-30-20-10", "tip": "Land softly with both feet and stand up fully on the box. Stepping down saves your legs.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Kettlebell Swings", "reps": "50-40-30-20-10", "tip": "Snap your hips and let the bell float. CrossFit''s standard swing finishes overhead.", "rx_men": "53 lb", "rx_women": "35 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Break the 50 wall balls before you have to", "Step down from the box every rep", "The sets shrink fast after the 30s"]'::jsonb,
   '["Plan the first round in sets, such as 20, 15 and 15 wall balls.", "Keep the box jumps steady; a missed jump costs more time than a slow one.", "On the swings, keep your arms loose and let your hips do the lifting.", "Take a breath at the top of each wall ball rather than resting with the ball on the floor.", "Push the pace from the set of 20 onward."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lighter ball, such as 14 lb / 10 lb, to a lower target, a 20 in / 16 in box or step-ups, and a lighter kettlebell. Swing to eye level if overhead swings bother your shoulders. Cut the ladder to 30-20-10 for a shorter workout.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Morrison workout?", "answer": "50-40-30-20-10 reps for time of wall balls (20 lb / 14 lb to 10 ft / 9 ft), box jumps (24 in / 20 in) and kettlebell swings (53 lb / 35 lb)."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Morrison?", "answer": "450 reps: 150 wall balls, 150 box jumps and 150 kettlebell swings."}, {"question": "Do the swings go overhead?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say on this workout. CrossFit''s standard kettlebell swing finishes with the bell overhead."}, {"question": "Who was Morrison?", "answer": "U.S. Army Spc. Scott Morrison, 23, of Blue Ash, Ohio. He died on Sept. 26, 2010, from injuries suffered when insurgents attacked his vehicle with an improvised explosive device in Kandahar, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
