   'time',
   'Muller honors firefighter James Michael Muller, 25, of the Irmo Fire District in Irmo, South Carolina. He died on May 26, 2023, when a building collapsed while he was fighting a fire. He started as a cadet in a high school program, graduated top of his class and was hired by the district.

You run 1,000 m and carry a plate (45 lb / 25 lb) 710 m. Then you do 5 rounds of 13 burpee pull-ups and 13 deadlifts (225 lb / 155 lb), carry the plate another 710 m and run a final 1,000 m. The long plate carries tire your grip and shoulders before and after the deadlifts. CrossFit does not say how to hold the plate, so choose a hold you can keep moving with.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "1,000 m", "tip": "Start easy. There is a long way to go."}, {"name": "Plate Run", "reps": "710 m carry", "tip": "CrossFit calls this a carry, so walking or running both count. It does not say how to hold the plate.", "rx_men": "45 lb plate", "rx_women": "25 lb plate"}, {"name": "Burpee Pull-Ups", "reps": "5 rounds of 13", "tip": "Do a burpee under the bar, jump up and pull until your chin clears the bar."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "5 rounds of 13", "tip": "Flat back, bar close to your legs. Break the set before your back rounds.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}, {"name": "Plate Run", "reps": "710 m carry", "tip": "Your grip is tired now. Switch holds often.", "rx_men": "45 lb plate", "rx_women": "25 lb plate"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "1,000 m", "tip": "The last effort. Shorten your stride and keep moving."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Switch your plate hold before your grip gives out", "Break the 13 deadlifts into smaller sets", "Run the first 1,000 m easy"]'::jsonb,
   '["Hug the plate to your chest when your grip tires; it saves your hands for the pull-ups and deadlifts.", "On the burpee pull-ups, jump into the pull so your legs do part of the work.", "Plan the deadlifts as sets, such as 5, 4 and 4, from the first round.", "Mark out the 710 m carry before you start so you do not lose count.", "Note which plate hold you used with your score, because CrossFit leaves it open."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lighter plate, such as 25 lb / 10 lb, and lower the deadlift to 155 lb / 105 lb or less. Replace burpee pull-ups with burpees and jumping pull-ups. Shorten the runs to 600 m and the carries to 400 m, or do 3 rounds in the middle.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Muller workout?", "answer": "For time: run 1,000 m, 710 m plate carry, then 5 rounds of 13 burpee pull-ups and 13 deadlifts, then a 710 m plate carry and a 1,000 m run. The plate is 45 lb / 25 lb and the deadlift is 225 lb / 155 lb."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Muller?", "answer": "130 reps: 65 burpee pull-ups and 65 deadlifts, plus 2,000 m of running and 1,420 m of plate carry."}, {"question": "How do I hold the plate?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Hold it any way you like and switch as your grip tires."}, {"question": "Who was Muller?", "answer": "James Michael Muller, 25, a firefighter with the Irmo Fire District in South Carolina. He died on May 26, 2023, when a building collapsed while he was fighting a fire."}]'::jsonb,
