   'time',
   'Nickman honors U.S. Army Spc. Nicholas B. Burley, 22, of Red Bluff, California, of the 6th Squadron, 8th Cavalry Regiment, 3rd Infantry Division. He died on July 30, 2013, in Logar Province, Afghanistan, from injuries caused by indirect fire.

Each of the 10 rounds is a 200 m farmers carry with two dumbbells (55 lb / 40 lb), 10 pull-ups with a dumbbell (35 lb / 20 lb) between your legs or on a belt, and 20 alternating dumbbell power snatches with the carry weight. That adds up to 2,000 m of carrying, 100 weighted pull-ups and 200 snatches. Every piece of it hits your grip, so the last rounds come down to how well you managed your hands.',
   '[{"name": "Farmers Carry", "reps": "200 m", "tip": "Stand tall, shoulders back, and walk fast. Put the dumbbells down before your grip fails, not after.", "rx_men": "2 × 55 lb", "rx_women": "2 × 40 lb"}, {"name": "Weighted Pull-Ups", "reps": "10", "tip": "Hold the dumbbell between your feet or on a belt. Chin clears the bar on every rep.", "rx_men": "35 lb", "rx_women": "20 lb"}, {"name": "Dumbbell Snatches", "reps": "20 alternating", "tip": "Power snatch one dumbbell from the floor to overhead in one motion, switching arms each rep.", "rx_men": "55 lb", "rx_women": "40 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Walk the carry fast instead of running it", "Break the pull-ups early", "Shake out your hands between movements"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set the pull-up dumbbell next to the bar so it is ready each round.", "Split the 10 weighted pull-ups into sets, such as 4, 3 and 3, from the first round.", "On the snatches, use your hips and keep the dumbbell close, then punch it to lockout.", "Count the 20 snatches as 20 total, alternating arms, which is 10 per arm.", "Use chalk and keep your grip relaxed on the carry, squeezing only as much as you need."]'::jsonb,
   'Use lighter dumbbells, such as 35 lb / 25 lb, for the carry and snatches. Do bodyweight pull-ups, or banded or jumping pull-ups, instead of weighted ones. Shorten the carry to 100 m, or do 5 rounds instead of 10.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Nickman workout?", "answer": "10 rounds for time of a 200 m farmers carry, 10 weighted pull-ups and 20 alternating dumbbell power snatches. Use 55 lb / 40 lb dumbbells for the carry and snatches and a 35 lb / 20 lb dumbbell for the pull-ups."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Nickman?", "answer": "300 reps: 100 weighted pull-ups and 200 dumbbell snatches, plus 2,000 m of farmers carry."}, {"question": "Are the 20 snatches per arm?", "answer": "No. They alternate arms, so it is 20 in total, 10 per arm."}, {"question": "Who was Nickman?", "answer": "U.S. Army Spc. Nicholas B. Burley, 22, of Red Bluff, California. He died on July 30, 2013, in Logar Province, Afghanistan, from injuries caused by indirect fire."}]'::jsonb,
