   'Northrup honors Detective Constable Jeffrey Northrup, 55, of the Toronto Police Service in Canada. He was killed in the line of duty on July 2, 2021, while investigating a stabbing. He mentored new officers, who called him "Papa Bear" and "Big Country," and he was a member of Heart and Hustle CrossFit.

One barbell (95 lb / 65 lb) does all the lifting. You start with 26 back-rack step-ups to a 24 in / 20 in box, then do 3 rounds of 17 power cleans, 19 sit-ups and 21 deadlifts, and finish with a 31-calorie row. The weight is light, so the challenge is moving fast for 51 power cleans and 63 deadlifts without long breaks.',
   '[{"name": "Barbell Step-Ups", "reps": "26", "tip": "Bar on your back, whole foot on the box, stand all the way up. CrossFit does not say whether reps count per leg.", "rx_men": "95 lb, 24 in", "rx_women": "65 lb, 20 in"}, {"name": "Power Cleans", "reps": "3 rounds of 17", "tip": "Catch the bar above parallel. Fast touch-and-go sets work at this weight.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}, {"name": "Sit-Ups", "reps": "3 rounds of 19", "tip": "Touch the floor behind you and reach past your toes at the top."}, {"name": "Deadlifts", "reps": "3 rounds of 21", "tip": "Flat back, bar close to your legs. Keep the reps moving.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}, {"name": "Row for Calories", "reps": "31 cal", "tip": "Sprint it. Long, strong strokes and push with the legs."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Keep the bar moving, the weight is light", "Do not rush the step-ups with a bar on your back", "Empty the tank on the row"]'::jsonb,
   '["Clean the bar from the floor and press or jerk it onto your back to start the step-ups.", "Count each time you stand on the box as one rep, because CrossFit does not say per leg.", "Break the 17 power cleans into two sets, such as 9 and 8, if you need to.", "Use the sit-ups to let your grip recover before the deadlifts.", "Have the rower set to calories before you start."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lighter barbell, such as 65 lb / 45 lb, or step up with no bar or to a lower box. Cut the rounds to 12 power cleans, 14 sit-ups and 15 deadlifts, or do 2 rounds instead of 3.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Northrup workout?", "answer": "For time: 26 barbell back-rack step-ups, then 3 rounds of 17 power cleans, 19 sit-ups and 21 deadlifts, then a 31-calorie row. The barbell is 95 lb / 65 lb and the box is 24 in / 20 in."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Northrup?", "answer": "197 reps: 26 step-ups, 51 power cleans, 57 sit-ups and 63 deadlifts, plus 31 calories on the rower."}, {"question": "Are the step-ups counted per leg?", "answer": "CrossFit does not say. Count each time you stand on the box as one rep and note it with your time."}, {"question": "Who was Northrup?", "answer": "Detective Constable Jeffrey Northrup, 55, of the Toronto Police Service. He was killed in the line of duty on July 2, 2021, while investigating a stabbing."}]'::jsonb,
