   array['running','box','pullUpBar','barbell','bodyweight']::text[],
   'time',
   'Nunez honors Deputy Andrew Nunez, 28, a San Bernardino County Sheriff''s Deputy assigned to the Rancho Cucamonga station. He died on Monday, Oct. 27, while responding to a domestic violence call. He was a valued member of CrossFit Rancho Cucamonga.

This chipper comes in three parts that get shorter and harder. First an 800 m run, 60 burpee box jump-overs, 50 pull-ups and 40 squats at 95 lb / 65 lb. Then a 600 m run, 30 burpee box jump-overs, 25 chest-to-bar pull-ups and 20 squats at 185 lb / 125 lb. Last, a 400 m run, 15 burpee box jump-overs, 12 bar muscle-ups and 10 squat cleans at 225 lb / 155 lb. The box is 20 in for everyone. The volume drops but the skill and the weight rise, so the end is the hardest part.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "800 m", "tip": "Start easy. A big set of burpees is waiting."}, {"name": "Burpee Box Jump-Over", "reps": "60", "tip": "Chest to the floor, then jump or step over the box. Keep a steady rhythm.", "rx_men": "20 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "50", "tip": "Chin clears the bar. Small sets from the start."}, {"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "40", "tip": "CrossFit only says squats, not back or front. Pick one style and use it for both squat sets.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "600 m", "tip": "Shake out your arms and legs."}, {"name": "Burpee Box Jump-Over", "reps": "30", "tip": "Same rhythm as the first set.", "rx_men": "20 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Chest-to-Bar Pull-Ups", "reps": "25", "tip": "Pull until your chest touches the bar."}, {"name": "Back Squats", "reps": "20", "tip": "Much heavier now. Break the set before your form slips.", "rx_men": "185 lb", "rx_women": "125 lb"}, {"name": "Run", "reps": "400 m", "tip": "The last run. Breathe before the final section."}, {"name": "Burpee Box Jump-Over", "reps": "15", "tip": "Get through these steadily.", "rx_men": "20 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "Bar Muscle-Up", "reps": "12", "tip": "Pull hard to your hips and press over the bar. Singles are fine."}, {"name": "Squat Cleans", "reps": "10", "tip": "Heavy. Take them as singles and set your back before every pull.", "rx_men": "225 lb", "rx_women": "155 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Hold back on the first 60 burpee box jump-overs", "Load the heavy bars before you start", "Expect the last section to take the longest"]'::jsonb,
   '["Set up three barbells, or plan quick plate changes, for the three squat loads.", "CrossFit lists the squats as weight 1 and weight 2 but does not name the style; use the same style for both sets and note it.", "Break the 50 pull-ups into sets of 10 or fewer so you have something left for chest-to-bar and muscle-ups.", "On the burpee box jump-overs, face the box and step down on the far side to save your legs.", "Treat the 10 squat cleans as heavy singles with a short, steady rest between each."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the squats to 65, 125 and 155 lb for men and 45, 85 and 105 lb for women, or less. Use a 20 in / 16 in box or step over it. Replace chest-to-bar with pull-ups and bar muscle-ups with chest-to-bar or jumping bar muscle-ups. Cut the burpee sets to 40, 20 and 10 and the pull-ups to 30 for a shorter workout.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Nunez workout?", "answer": "For time: 800 m run, 60 burpee box jump-overs, 50 pull-ups, 40 squats; 600 m run, 30 burpee box jump-overs, 25 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 20 squats; 400 m run, 15 burpee box jump-overs, 12 bar muscle-ups, 10 squat cleans. The box is 20 in. Loads are 95, 185 and 225 lb for men and 65, 125 and 155 lb for women."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Nunez?", "answer": "262 reps: 105 burpee box jump-overs, 50 pull-ups, 25 chest-to-bar pull-ups, 12 bar muscle-ups, 60 squats and 10 squat cleans, plus 1,800 m of running."}, {"question": "What kind of squats are they?", "answer": "CrossFit only says squats. Back squats or front squats both fit the wording, so pick one and note it with your time."}, {"question": "Who was Nunez?", "answer": "Deputy Andrew Nunez, 28, a San Bernardino County Sheriff''s Deputy. He died on Monday, Oct. 27, while responding to a domestic violence call."}]'::jsonb,
   null),
  ('ODA 7313',
   'oda-7313',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   '7 Rounds For Time',
   '20–30 min',
   'intermediate',
   'full-body',
   array['running','dumbbells','pullUpBar']::text[],
   'time',
   'ODA 7313 honors U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Javier Jaguar Gutierrez, 28, of Jacksonville, North Carolina, a Special Forces communications sergeant with the 3rd Battalion, 7th Special Forces Group (Airborne). He died on Feb. 8, 2020, from wounds sustained during combat operations in Nangarhar Province, Afghanistan.

Each of the 7 rounds is a 300 m jog, 10 single-arm dumbbell thrusters on the left, 10 on the right and 7 strict pull-ups. The dumbbell is 30 lb / 20 lb. That adds up to 2,100 m of jogging, 140 thrusters and 49 strict pull-ups. The weight is light, but holding one dumbbell asks a lot of your trunk, and strict pull-ups add up quickly with no kip to help.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "300 m jog", "tip": "CrossFit calls it a jog, so keep it relaxed and use it to recover."}, {"name": "Dumbbell Thrusters", "reps": "10 left arm", "tip": "One dumbbell on your left shoulder. Squat below parallel and drive it straight overhead.", "rx_men": "30 lb", "rx_women": "20 lb"}, {"name": "Dumbbell Thrusters", "reps": "10 right arm", "tip": "Switch the dumbbell to your right shoulder. Keep your chest up and do not lean.", "rx_men": "30 lb", "rx_women": "20 lb"}, {"name": "Pull-Ups", "reps": "7 strict", "tip": "No kip. Start from a dead hang and pull until your chin clears the bar."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Keep the jog easy", "Squeeze your trunk on the single-arm thrusters", "Split the strict pull-ups early if you need to"]'::jsonb,
   '["Keep your free arm out to the side for balance during the thrusters.", "Stack the dumbbell over your shoulder at the top, with your biceps by your ear.", "On strict pull-ups, start each rep from straight arms and keep your legs still.", "Break the 7 pull-ups into 4 and 3 from the start if 7 strict reps are close to your max.", "Hold the same jog pace every round so you can tell when you are slowing down."]'::jsonb,
   'Use a lighter dumbbell, such as 20 lb / 15 lb. Replace strict pull-ups with banded pull-ups or ring rows, or cut them to 4 per round. Shorten the jog to 200 m or do 5 rounds instead of 7.',
   '[{"question": "What is the ODA 7313 workout?", "answer": "7 rounds for time of a 300 m jog, 10 left-arm dumbbell thrusters, 10 right-arm dumbbell thrusters and 7 strict pull-ups. The dumbbell is 30 lb / 20 lb."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in ODA 7313?", "answer": "189 reps: 140 single-arm thrusters (70 per arm) and 49 strict pull-ups, plus 2,100 m of jogging."}, {"question": "Do I need one dumbbell or two?", "answer": "One. Each thruster set is done with a single dumbbell on one side, then the other."}, {"question": "Who was ODA 7313 named for?", "answer": "U.S. Army Sgt. 1st Class Javier Jaguar Gutierrez, 28, a Special Forces communications sergeant with the 7th Special Forces Group (Airborne). He died on Feb. 8, 2020, from wounds sustained in Nangarhar Province, Afghanistan."}]'::jsonb,
   null),
  ('Omar',
   'omar',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   'For Time',
   '12–20 min',
   'intermediate',
   'full-body',
   array['barbell','bodyweight']::text[],
   'time',
   'Omar honors U.S. Army 1st Lt. Omar Vazquez, 25, of Hamilton, New Jersey, of the 2nd Squadron, 3rd Armored Cavalry Regiment. He died of wounds suffered on April 22, 2011, when insurgents attacked his unit with an improvised explosive device in Numaniyah, Iraq.

You alternate thrusters (95 lb / 65 lb) and bar-facing burpees in sets that climb: 10 thrusters, 15 burpees, 20 thrusters, 25 burpees, 30 thrusters and 35 burpees. That is 60 thrusters and 75 burpees. Unlike most chippers, the sets get bigger as you get tired, so the last 30 thrusters and 35 burpees decide your time.',
   '[{"name": "Thrusters", "reps": "10-20-30", "tip": "Front squat below parallel and drive the bar straight overhead in one motion.", "rx_men": "95 lb", "rx_women": "65 lb"}, {"name": "Bar-Facing Burpees", "reps": "15-25-35", "tip": "Chest to the floor facing the bar, then jump over it with both feet."}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Go easy on the first two sets", "Break the 30 thrusters into a plan", "Stay low on the burpee jumps"]'::jsonb,
   '["Do the first 10 thrusters unbroken, then plan the 30 as sets, such as 10, 10 and 10.", "Keep your elbows high in the front rack so the bar does not pull you forward.", "On the bar-facing burpees, jump just high enough to clear the bar.", "Land facing the bar each time so you do not waste steps turning around.", "Push the pace on the last 35 burpees; there is nothing left to save energy for."]'::jsonb,
   'Lower the barbell to 65 lb / 45 lb or use dumbbells. Step over the bar instead of jumping. Halve each set (5, 8, 10, 13, 15, 18) for a shorter workout.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Omar workout?", "answer": "For time: 10 thrusters, 15 bar-facing burpees, 20 thrusters, 25 bar-facing burpees, 30 thrusters and 35 bar-facing burpees. The barbell is 95 lb / 65 lb."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Omar?", "answer": "135 reps: 60 thrusters and 75 bar-facing burpees."}, {"question": "Who was Omar?", "answer": "U.S. Army 1st Lt. Omar Vazquez, 25, of Hamilton, New Jersey. He died of wounds suffered on April 22, 2011, when insurgents attacked his unit with an improvised explosive device in Numaniyah, Iraq."}]'::jsonb,
   'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BFXF8crKLxA'),
  ('Operation Red Wings',
   'operation-red-wings',
   'hero',
   null,
   'For Time',
   'For Time',
   '25–40 min',
   'intermediate',
   'full-body',
   array['running','pullUpBar','box','kettlebell','bodyweight']::text[],
   'time',
   'Operation Red Wings honors the U.S. service members killed during Operation Red Wings in Kunar Province, Afghanistan, on June 28, 2005. Three of the four Navy SEALs on a reconnaissance team, Lt. Michael P. Murphy, Gunner''s Mate 2nd Class Danny Dietz and Sonar Technician 2nd Class Matthew Axelson, were killed on the ground. Eight more Navy SEALs and eight Army Night Stalkers were killed when their MH-47 Chinook was shot down trying to reach them.

Each part of the workout stands for part of that day. The ¾-mile (1,200 m) run is for the three SEALs killed on the ground. The 16 rounds of 8 toes-to-bar and 8 burpee box jump-overs (24 in / 20 in) are for the 16 service members on the helicopter: eight Night Stalkers and eight SEALs. The 47 goblet squats (70 lb / 53 lb) are for the MH-47.',
   '[{"name": "Run", "reps": "1,200 m", "tip": "Three-quarters of a mile. Hold a pace that leaves room for 16 rounds."}, {"name": "Toes-to-Bar", "reps": "16 rounds of 8", "tip": "Hang from the bar and touch both feet to it between your hands. Short sets keep your grip fresh."}, {"name": "Burpee Box Jump-Over", "reps": "16 rounds of 8", "tip": "Chest to the floor, then jump or step over the box.", "rx_men": "24 in", "rx_women": "20 in"}, {"name": "KB Goblet Squats", "reps": "47", "tip": "Hold the kettlebell at your chest, elbows inside your knees, and squat below parallel.", "rx_men": "70 lb", "rx_women": "53 lb"}]'::jsonb,
   'Record your finish time.',
   '["Pace the 16 rounds, not the run", "Split the toes-to-bar early", "Break the 47 squats into a few sets"]'::jsonb,
   '["Pick a steady pace for the rounds, such as one round every 1:15, and hold it.", "On toes-to-bar, use a small kip and squeeze your lats to keep the swing short.", "Step down off the box on the far side of the burpee box jump-overs to save your legs.", "Keep your chest up and the kettlebell tight to you on the goblet squats.", "Break the 47 goblet squats into sets, such as 15, 12, 10 and 10."]'::jsonb,
   'Replace toes-to-bar with hanging knee raises, use a lower box or step over it, and use a lighter kettlebell, such as 53 lb / 35 lb. Cut the rounds to 8 instead of 16 or the reps to 5 per round for a shorter workout, and keep the 47 goblet squats if you can.',
   '[{"question": "What is the Operation Red Wings workout?", "answer": "For time: ¾-mile (1,200 m) run, then 16 rounds of 8 toes-to-bar and 8 burpee box jump-overs (24 in / 20 in), then 47 goblet squats (70 lb / 53 lb)."}, {"question": "How many total reps are in Operation Red Wings?", "answer": "303 reps: 128 toes-to-bar, 128 burpee box jump-overs and 47 goblet squats, plus a 1,200 m run."}, {"question": "What do the numbers mean?", "answer": "The ¾-mile run is for the three SEALs killed on the ground. The 16 rounds are for the 16 service members killed in the rescue attempt, with 8 toes-to-bar for the eight Night Stalkers and 8 burpee box jump-overs for the eight SEALs. The 47 goblet squats are for the MH-47 Chinook."}, {"question": "Who does Operation Red Wings honor?", "answer": "The U.S. service members killed during Operation Red Wings in Kunar Province, Afghanistan, on June 28, 2005: three Navy SEALs on the ground, and eight Navy SEALs and eight Army Night Stalkers aboard the MH-47 Chinook that was shot down trying to reach them."}]'::jsonb,
   null);
  get diagnostics n = row_count;
  if n <> 12 then raise exception 'expected % inserts', 12; end if;
end $$;

select slug, scheme from benchmark_workouts where slug in ('mccartney', 'meadows', 'miron', 'monti', 'morrison', 'muller', 'nickman', 'northrup', 'nunez', 'oda-7313', 'omar', 'operation-red-wings') order by slug;
